From 2409d14791f2ae3651cf6489d94a706968c0a8eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Bockelie <aaronsb@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:39:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: ratelimit the repeated-handover
 message

On SM8450 the SLPI toggles its SMP2P ready and handover bits at the
sensor sample rate while a sensor session is open (issue #46). Every
edge after the first lands in q6v5_handover_interrupt with
handover_issued set and prints "Handover signaled, but it already
happened" at error level. With the folio-state daemon sampling the
magnetometer and light sensor this fills the console and wraps the
kernel ring buffer within minutes, which has already cost resume traces
(#51). The condition is harmless and the handler returns early; the
message stays, rate limited.

Upstream shape: the same one-line change, or a dev_dbg, in
drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c.

[Taken unchanged from github.com/aaronsb/sm-x800-linux
 pmaports-overlay/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-sm8450/q6v5-handover-ratelimit.patch
 (main 6f32485, GPL-2.0-only); the diting SLPI shows the same
 (633 messages within a minute of sensor use).]
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 241478ea2..5dd00fd0d 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_err_ratelimited(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
